                <h2><strong>Selected Work &amp; Impact</strong></h2>
                <h3><strong>Geospatial Platforms &amp; Data Infrastructure</strong></h3>
                <p>I architected <strong>MapHub</strong>, an early real-time collaborative environment for map editing that became foundational infrastructure for multiple internal and external products. Working closely with a small, highly capable engineering team, I shaped backend services, standardized data models, and introduced interaction patterns that made large-scale spatial data tangible and editable in near real time.</p>
                <p>At Nokia, this work scaled into <strong>Nokia Map Creator</strong>, a public map-editing platform that significantly expanded global map coverage. Alongside community contribution, we built moderation, review, and partner data ingestion workflows that balanced openness with data quality.</p>
                <p>Later, I led the technical and organizational coordination required to launch <strong>HERE XYZ</strong>, a modular geospatial data platform with a low-code/no-code editor (XYZ Studio). We released the platform with both HERE and OpenStreetMap base data and open-sourced the full ecosystem — including SDKs, command-line tools, and AI/ML integrations — enabling developers to run or host their own XYZ instances.</p>
                <p>I was a founding member of the <strong>Linux Foundation Urban Computing Foundation</strong>, initially serving on the Steering Group to help shape open standards for urban data platforms.</p>
                <hr>
                <h3><strong>Platform Leadership &amp; Developer Engagement</strong></h3>
                <p>From 2017 onward, my focus expanded toward platform leadership and ecosystem development. I coordinated engineering teams across Frankfurt, Mumbai, and San Francisco, worked closely with the Open Source Program Office in Berlin, and collaborated with stakeholders across Europe and the U.S.</p>
                <p>Following the public launch of HERE XYZ, I increasingly represented the platform externally — delivering sessions and keynotes at events such as WeAreDevelopers, FOSSGIS / FOSS4G, the Linux Foundation Open Source Summit, and Embedded Linux Conference Europe. I also supported numerous hackathons and developer initiatives, helping teams turn ideas into working prototypes.</p>
                <p>In 2021, HERE decided to significantly reduce its open-source activities. As open collaboration had been a core motivator for both the teams and myself, this marked a natural transition point.</p>
                <hr>
                <h3><strong>Entrepreneurship, Open Source &amp; Quiet Tech</strong></h3>
                <p>After leaving HERE, I founded <strong>lemon slice digital GmbH</strong> to focus on building thoughtful, sustainable digital products — from bespoke web and mobile systems to AI-driven platforms. The company also maintains a fully open-source fork of <strong>XYZmaps</strong> as a geospatial and earth-observation data platform and holds the EU trademark for “XYZ maps”.</p>
                <p>To support focused exploration and product craftsmanship, lemon slice digital operates several internal initiatives:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Lemon Slice Labs</strong> — experimental R&amp;D, including evolutionary AI-assisted software development (REI Project)</li>
                    <li><strong>Lemon Slice Studios</strong> — refined Android experiences and product design</li>
                    <li><strong>XYZ Maps</strong> - a free and open source mapping and earth data platform</li>
                    <li><strong>Ambiance</strong> — a dynamic, theme-aware Android wallpaper application</li>
                </ul>
                <hr>
                <h3><strong>AI-Driven Product Innovation</strong></h3>
                <p>As Technology Partner at <strong>LevaData</strong>, I helped modernize architecture, infrastructure, and user experience, enabling more scalable AI-driven insights.</p>
                <p>As Fractional CTO at <strong>Braided Health</strong>, I designed and guided the development of an AI-enabled care management platform supporting complex, dual-eligible healthcare environments. The work focused on augmenting care coordinators, improving system coherence, and building technology that fits the realities of healthcare delivery.</p>
                <p>I also created <strong>SenpAI</strong>, a real-time conversational and contextual AI that provides subtle, context-aware guidance during audio and video calls, currently deployed in early production environments.</p>
